2. Problems Discovered and Fixes Applied
Problem: Objects registered with LODSystem would instantly toggle their visibility (.visible = true / false) at the exact distance boundary. When the camera drifted slightly back and forth across the threshold, objects would rapidly pop in and out of view (flickering).
Fix: Implemented Distance Hysteresis in LODSystem.update():
TypeScript
const threshold = entry.currentVisible ? scaledMaxDist : scaledMaxDist * 0.92;
const inRange = distSq < threshold * threshold;
Once an object hides, the camera must move 8% closer (scaledMaxDist * 0.92) for it to reappear, completely eliminating boundary flickering while preserving the throttled 200ms mobile update interval.
